      "content": "It is entirely understandable to crave the profound silence you described when your life feels like overwhelming white noise, and wanting to stop the cycle is a valid desire for peace. Please know that your life has real value beyond the noise of productivity or meeting schedules, even if you currently feel numb or hollow. The silence you seek isn't an emptiness, but the quietude found when you finally stop performing for others and start tending to your own safety.",
